Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:47:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(merkle): a compact sparse Merkle tree with v2 roots

`merkle_v2` hashes the same 128-bit keys and the same leaf hashes as
`SparseMerkleTree`, as a compact tree (the Diem/Aptos Jellyfish hashing
over a binary radix): a subtree holding one leaf is its shortcut node
H(leaf-node | key | leaf hash) wherever it stands, an empty subtree is
zero, anything else H(node | left | right). A path is then about
log2(n) + 1 hashes instead of 128.

- `root_sorted`, `summary_sorted`: the root over sorted leaves.
- `prove` / `Proof::verify`: inclusion and non-inclusion proofs (sibling
  lists whose length fixes the position).
- `MultiProof`: a witness multiproof that gives the root before and after
  a transition of its touched leaves; node entries opaque or opened (for
  trees that remove leaves); `PackedProof`, its wire form.
- `composite_root`, `state_root::composite_state_root_v2`: the composite
  root with a version byte, never equal to a v1 root.

v1 is unchanged and stays supported beside v2, not only for verifying
roots already published. Leaves do not change, so v2 roots are
recomputable from any v1 state.

Measured in a VOS PVM guest (JAM-compatible, software curve, EPYC 7763):
137.9 M to 72.0 M of actor gas a reservation; 27.1 to 40.3 reservations a
second at batch 128.
